    "updated_at": "2018-07-31T13:41:20Z",
    "body": "```\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n...<script>\r\ni = 0;\r\nclass CustomElement extends HTMLElement {\r\n  constructor() {\r\n    w(i++);\r\n  }\r\n};\r\ncustomElements.define(\"custom-element\", CustomElement);\r\n</script>\r\n<custom-element></custom-element>\r\n<script>\r\ndocument.body.appendChild(document.querySelector(\"custom-element\"));\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\nthis ends up logging 0 and an exception in Live DOM Viewer for me. In both Chrome and Firefox. That means upgrading only happened once, right? In Safari the exception isn't logged, but 0 is.\r\n\r\nIt seems that would mean upgrading isn't attempted again, whereas the current specification says it would happen again.",
